---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import portrait from '../assets/portrait.png';
import design from '../assets/creative.png';
import photo from '../assets/photography.jpg';
import { href } from '../lib/paths';
---
<Base title="About" active="about"><div class="wrap inner-page"><header class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">KENYAN / BASED IN MAURITIUS</p><h1>A little more<br />human<span class="red-dot">.</span></h1></header><div class="about-main"><div class="prose"><p>I’m Simon Mwaura, an engineer with a growing interest in complex systems and data-driven decision-making.</p><p>I started in electrical systems engineering. Today, I work as a Research and Analytics Engineer at Werttax International Ltd, supporting the adaptation of German valuation methodologies and analytical tools to the Mauritian real-estate market.</p><p>My interests span optimisation, statistical learning, dynamic systems, state estimation, and control. Software is one way I explore those interests; learning is a continuing part of the process.</p><p>There’s also a creative thread: graphic design, photography, and INCOGNITO. Different ways of paying attention, experimenting, and making something of an idea.</p><p><a href={href('cv/')}>Read my CV ↗</a></p></div><Image src={portrait} alt="Black-and-white portrait of Simon Mwaura." width={600} format="webp" /></div><section id="creative" class="about-creative"><p class="eyebrow">ANOTHER SIDE OF THE SAME CURIOSITY</p><h2>Outside the brief<span class="red-dot">.</span></h2><p>Some of my earlier creative work: graphics, visual experiments, and moments behind a camera. A few pieces from the college years that still feel like part of the story.</p><div class="creative-strip"><Image src={design} alt="Go With the Flow: a colourful abstract graphic from Simon’s creative portfolio." width={900} format="webp" loading="lazy" /><Image src={photo} alt="Street photography from Simon’s college-era portfolio." width={900} format="webp" loading="lazy" /></div></section></div></Base>
